---
import SectionHeading from "./SectionHeading.astro";
---

<section
  id="about"
  data-section-name="About"
  tabindex="-1"
  aria-label="About Manvendra Rajpoot"
  class="section-reveal mb-28 max-w-180 text-center leading-8 outline-none sm:mb-40 scroll-mt-28"
>
  <SectionHeading>About me</SectionHeading>

  <p class="mb-3">
    I'm a <span class="font-medium">backend developer</span> who enjoys building systems
    that are <span class="font-medium"
      >scalable, secure, and quietly reliable</span
    >. Across my roles at <span class="font-medium">CloudTechTiq</span> and <span
      class="font-medium">Radixlink</span
    >, I've designed and shipped multi-tenant SaaS platforms, central
    authentication systems with multi-factor auth and role-based access, payment
    integrations across <span class="font-medium"
      >Stripe, Razorpay and PayPal</span
    >, and <span class="font-medium">AI-powered features</span> — from automated invoice
    extraction to grammar correction in customer support. My core stack is <span
      class="font-medium">Python, Django, DRF and FastAPI</span
    >, backed by <span class="font-medium">PostgreSQL, Redis and MongoDB</span>,
    and shipped with <span class="font-medium"
      >Docker, Kubernetes and CI/CD</span
    >. <span class="italic">My favorite part of the job</span> is the problem-solving
    — turning a messy, manual process into a clean, automated system that just works.
  </p>

  <p>
    I care most about the things users never notice: <span class="font-medium"
      >API security</span
    >, real-time notifications, background-job systems, and disaster-recovery
    plans that keep data safe and services running. On the frontend I work with <span
      class="font-medium">React, Next.js and TypeScript</span
    >, so I can take a feature from the database all the way to the browser. I'm
    currently pursuing my <span class="font-medium"
      >Master of Computer Applications</span
    > at Jain University after completing my BCA at Bundelkhand University, and I
    never stop <span class="underline">learning</span> — a new framework, a cloud
    service, or a better way to architect a backend. I'm open to <a
      href="#contact"
      class="font-medium underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-gray-950 dark:hover:text-white"
      >backend and full-stack roles</a
    > where I can build things that scale.
  </p>
</section>
